---
// Privacy Policy — traduction de src/pages/politique-de-confidentialite.astro.
// Même écart assumé que la version FR : le site charge Google Analytics
// derrière CookieConsent, donc les sections 5, 6 et 8 décrivent ce
// comportement réel plutôt que la maquette d'origine. Si Google Analytics
// est un jour retiré du Layout, ce sont ces sections (dans les deux langues)
// qu'il faut reprendre.
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../../styles/legal.css";
---

<Layout
  lang="en"
  title="Privacy Policy · IZYBIZ"
  description="IZYBIZ privacy policy: data collected, purposes, retention periods, processors and how to exercise your rights."
  canonicalPath="/en/privacy-policy/"
>
  <main class="legal-page" data-section="legal">
    <h1 class="legal-page__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-page__updated">LAST UPDATED: 13-08-2026</p>
    <p class="legal-page__intro">
      This policy explains what data IZYBIZ collects when you use the
      visibility diagnosis and the Izy software, why it is collected, how
      long it is kept, and how to exercise your rights.
    </p>

    <div class="legal-page__body">
      <section>
        <h2 class="legal-page__heading">1. Data controller</h2>
        <p class="legal-page__text">
          IZYBIZ, a SASU (French simplified single-shareholder joint-stock
          company) with capital of €1,000, registered with the Paris Trade
          and Companies Register (RCS) under number 903 392 892. Registered
          office SIRET: 903 392 892 00019. Intra-EU VAT number:
          FR46903392892. Registered office: 361 rue Lecourbe, 75015 Paris,
          France. Contact:
          <a href="mailto:contact.me@izybiz.fr">contact.me@izybiz.fr</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="legal-page__heading">2. Data collected</h2>
        <div class="legal-page__cards">
          <div class="legal-page__card">
            <div class="legal-page__card-title">Visibility diagnosis</div>
            <p class="legal-page__card-text">
              Your website address and email address, along with
              information publicly available on your site and in the search
              results analyzed to produce the report.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="legal-page__card">
            <div class="legal-page__card-title">Contact form</div>
            <p class="legal-page__card-text">
              Your name, company, email address, website address, the
              subject of your request and the content of your message. This
              information is only used to reply to you.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="legal-page__card">
            <div class="legal-page__card-title">Account and mission</div>
            <p class="legal-page__card-text">
              Name, work email, company and role; the content of exchanges
              with Izy; the documents and information you provide as part of
              the mission.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="legal-page__card">
            <div class="legal-page__card-title">Technical data</div>
            <p class="legal-page__card-text">
              Connection logs, IP address and browser type, solely for
              security purposes and abuse prevention.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="legal-page__card">
            <div class="legal-page__card-title">Audience measurement</div>
            <p class="legal-page__card-text">
              If you consent: pages viewed, time spent, traffic source and
              associated technical data, collected via Google Analytics.
              Without your consent, none of this data is collected.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="legal-page__heading">3. Purposes and legal bases</h2>
        <ul class="legal-page__list">
          <li>
            Producing your diagnosis and sending you the result: performance
            of a contract or legitimate interest.
          </li>
          <li>
            Responding to a request submitted via the contact form:
            pre-contractual measures taken at your request, or legitimate
            interest.
          </li>
          <li>
            Executing the subscribed mission: audit, optimization,
            monitoring, writing, reporting: performance of a contract.
          </li>
          <li>Ensuring the security of the service and preventing abuse: legitimate interest.</li>
          <li>
            Measuring site traffic to improve its content: consent,
            revocable at any time.
          </li>
          <li>
            Sending you commercial information about our services: consent,
            revocable at any time.
          </li>
          <li>Complying with our accounting and legal obligations: legal obligation.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="legal-page__heading">4. Retention periods</h2>
        <ul class="legal-page__list">
          <li>Diagnosis data without subscription: twelve months from the request.</li>
          <li>Prospects with no follow-up: three years after your last contact.</li>
          <li>
            Account and mission data: for the duration of the contractual
            relationship, then five years for evidentiary purposes.
          </li>
          <li>Accounting records: ten years, in accordance with the law.</li>
          <li>Technical logs: six months.</li>
          <li>Audience measurement data: fourteen months maximum.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="legal-page__heading">5. Recipients and processors</h2>
        <p class="legal-page__text">
          Your data is accessible to authorized IZYBIZ staff and to the
          technical providers who work on our behalf: hosting (Netlify),
          email delivery (Zoho Mail), audience measurement (Google
          Analytics, only if you have consented) and artificial intelligence
          model providers. This last category changes depending on the
          models used: the up-to-date list of providers concerned is
          available on request at
          <a href="mailto:contact.me@izybiz.fr">contact.me@izybiz.fr</a>.
          These providers act on our instructions and are bound by a data
          processing agreement. No data is sold, and your content is not
          used to train models.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="legal-page__heading">6. Transfers outside the European Union</h2>
        <p class="legal-page__text">
          Some providers, notably Netlify and Google, may process data
          outside the European Union. These transfers are governed by the
          European Commission's standard contractual clauses or by an
          adequacy decision — for providers based in the United States,
          certification under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework. Details are
          available on request at
          <a href="mailto:contact.me@izybiz.fr">contact.me@izybiz.fr</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="legal-page__heading">7. Your rights</h2>
        <p class="legal-page__text">
          You have the right to access, rectify, erase, restrict and object
          to the processing of your data, as well as the right to data
          portability and to withdraw your consent. Write to
          <a href="mailto:contact.me@izybiz.fr">contact.me@izybiz.fr</a>:
          you will receive a reply within one month. You may also lodge a
          complaint with the CNIL (the French data protection authority).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="legal-page__heading">8. Cookies</h2>
        <p class="legal-page__text">
          This site sets two categories of cookies. Cookies strictly
          necessary for its operation and for the security of your session
          are set without consent, as the law does not require it. Google
          Analytics audience-measurement cookies (<code>_ga</code>,
          <code>_ga_*</code>, thirteen months) are only set after your
          explicit consent, collected via the banner shown on your first
          visit: until you accept, no measurement is performed.
        </p>
        <p class="legal-page__text">
          You can change or withdraw this choice at any time using the
          "Cookie settings" button permanently available on the site. No
          advertising or third-party tracking cookies are set.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="legal-page__heading">9. Security</h2>
        <p class="legal-page__text">
          Access is authenticated and logged, data is encrypted in transit,
          and permissions are limited to those who need them to carry out
          the mission.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="legal-page__heading">10. Changes</h2>
        <p class="legal-page__text">
          This policy may evolve. In the event of a significant change, you
          will be notified by email or through a message in the software
          before it takes effect.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-page__links">
      <a href="/en/">Back to home</a>
      <a href="/en/legal-notice/">Legal Notice</a>
      <a href="mailto:contact.me@izybiz.fr">Email us</a>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
